✅ What is JPA?

JPA (Java Persistence API) is a standard specification that defines how Java objects (entities)
are mapped to / stored in / retrieved from a relational database.

➡️ JPA is NOT a framework — it is a set of interfaces + annotations (API / contract).
➡️ You need a provider implementation: Hibernate (most common), EclipseLink, OpenJPA, etc.

Today’s package name:
- Older: javax.persistence.*
- Spring Boot 3+ / Jakarta EE: jakarta.persistence.*
(Often still called “JPA” in interviews.)

────────────────────────────────────────
🔸 JPA vs Hibernate (short)

| Feature  | JPA                     | Hibernate             |
| -------- | ----------------------- | --------------------- |
| Type     | Specification / API     | Implementation of JPA |
| Use      | Common portable API     | Actual ORM engine     |
| Alone?   | Needs a provider        | Is a provider         |

